In article <wZhHHwa00XoAQM6kRJ@andrew.cmu.edu> Ronald Eugene Snyder, II asks:
>1)  I zapped myself with a wand of make invisible, and became "invisible
>to others" according to a potion of self knowledge.  I was previously
>unaware of any state of visibility other than plain visible or
>invisible. What other kinds of invisibility are there, and what are the
>effects of having that kind of invisibility?  How does one get different
>kinds of invisibility.  I was playing an Elf and since elves have
>intrisic see invisible, is that why I was invisible to others and not to
>myself?  What happens if your invisible but can't see invisible?

If you can see invisibles, then you can see yourself.
Others you can't. However cursor shows where you are (in 3.0), so it
isn't any problem.
It is very good to be invisible because many monsters miss often when
they try to hit you.

>2)  How long does invisibility last, and is there anyway to terminate it
>before it's supposed to end?

Invisibility by wand seems to last forever and I don't know any way to
terminate it.

>3)  I couldn't enter a shop while invisible because the shop keeper was
>standing in the way.  What ways are there to get around this problem,
>and what are there effects?  (like hurting your alignment status,
>getting the shop keeper to attack you, or getting the Keystone Kops
>after you)

There some ways: 
1.) Shopkeeper stays at other side of the door when you are invisible.
You can kill him by zapping or throwing items. Kops don't care about
killing and if there is no more owner of all of those things...
However this decreases your luck.

2.) You can make a hole to the shop. Don't do it near the shopkeeper,
maybe he doesn't like it.

3.) Teleport inside and out.

If you get inside without killing the shopokeeper, you can bye the
objects if you wish.
